{"id":"n1-127","title":"Verb たら Verb たで (~ tara ~ tade)","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Conveys that if something happens (or doesn’t happen), there is a particular consequence or situation either way.","longExplanation":"The pattern VerbたらVerbたで is used for scenarios where doing something creates a certain issue or reaction, and not doing it also creates a different concern. It often shows that no matter which side of the condition you end up on, there’s some related result or trouble.","formation":"Verb-た form + ら + (same Verb-た form) + で","examples":[{"jp":"行ったら行ったで大変だし、行かなかったら行かなかったで後悔しそうだ。","romaji":"Ittara itta de taihen da shi, ikanakattara ikanakatta de kōkai shisō da.","en":"If I go, it’s a hassle; if I don’t go, I’ll regret it.","words":[{"surface":"行っ","vocabId":"1578850","reading":"いく","baseForm":"行く"},{"surface":"たら","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"た"},{"surface":"行っ","vocabId":"1578850","reading":"いく","baseForm":"行く"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"大変","vocabId":"1415000","reading":"たいへん"},{"surface":"だ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":null},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"行か","vocabId":"1578850","reading":"いく","baseForm":"行く"},{"surface":"なかっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ない"},{"surface":"たら","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"た"},{"surface":"行か","vocabId":"1578850","reading":"いく","baseForm":"行く"},{"surface":"なかっ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ない"},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"で","vocabId":null},{"surface":"後悔","vocabId":"1269510","reading":"こうかい"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"そう","vocabId":"1399540","reading":"そう"},{"surface":"だ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[1,4]},{"jp":"買ったら買ったでお金がなくなるし、買わなかったら買わなかったで後で欲しくなる。","romaji":"Kattara katta de okane ga naku naru shi, kawanakattara kawanakatta de ato de hoshiku naru.","en":"If I buy it, I’ll run out of money; if I don’t buy it, I’ll want it later.","words":[